r and nothing opens.\n\n**Closing it:** the caller uses the returned function. Calling it marks the instance `TO_BE_DELETED`. The store handler then calls `onClose`, unmounts the parcel, and removes the frame. The modal also closes on Escape and when the caller passes `close` through props. Inside the modal, the `close` prop is injected by `showModal` and can be called directly.\n\n**Documentation**\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/showModal.md` (lines 9–40): the public contract, including the `routes.json` requirement and the returned dispose function.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/API.md` (line 186): index entry for `showModal`.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/interfaces/OpenmrsAppRoutes.md` (lines 41–47): the `modals` route section, \"Modals can be launched by name\".\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-globals/src/types.ts` (lines 191–203): `ModalDefinition` (`name`, `component`).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/modals/index.tsx`:\n  - `ModalProps` (lines 10–13).\n  - `showModal` (lines 293–319): builds the `close` closure, which finds the instance by its `onClose` reference and calls `closeInstance`. It returns `close`.\n  - `renderModalIntoDOM` (lines 49–81): loads the lifecycle and renders it as a parcel into a frame.\n  - `handleModalStateUpdate` (lines 123–224): mounts `NEW` instances. On `TO_BE_DELETED` it runs `onClose`, unmounts the parcel, and removes the frame.\n  - `openInstance` (lines 226–234) and `closeInstance` (lines 236–250).\n  - `handleEscKey` and `closeHighestInstance` (lines 252–265).\n  - `setupModals` (lines 271–278).\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-extensions/src/modals.ts`:\n  - `registerModal` (lines 22–27) and `getModalRegistration` (lines 30–48). The lookup falls back to a deprecated extension registration with a warning.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/